FINDINGS:

1. [BLOCKER] src/lsp.rs:2555 — `find_references` only enters interpolation handling when the queried offset itself is inside a text literal. Queried from the declaration side (the normal "find all references" action), it falls through to `references_for`, which walks `analysis.tokens`; the whole `"…{greeting}…"` literal is one `TokenKind::Text` token there, so the interpolated use is invisible. The phase claims "find-references now look inside a `{…}` text interpolation", but a use inside the interpolation is only found when the query starts inside it: `find_references("set greeting to \"hi\"\nsay \"message: {greeting}\"\n", 1, 5)` returns only `(1,5)`, omitting `(2,16)`. New tests only query from inside the literal (`tests/tooling_grammar_test.rs:4496`, `:4564`), so the asymmetry is unpinned. Fix: after collecting references in the non-text path, resolve each text literal's interpolations and merge the mapped locations (or make reference collection globally interpolation-aware), and add a declaration-side test. — VERIFIED: traced `find_references` (src/lsp.rs:2550–2563): `inside_text` guards only the query offset, then the non-text branch calls `references_for` (src/lsp.rs:2565), whose loop at src/lsp.rs:2583 iterates `analysis.tokens`; `text_literal_at`/`decode_text_literal` (src/lsp.rs:2884, 2897) exist precisely because the lexer emits the whole literal as one token.

2. [MAJOR] phases/phase-075/REPORT.md:401 — the gate table now claims `cargo test --all-targets | 2883 passed`, and the prose at :404 says this is "the previous full-gate count plus the six resumed-run interpolation-navigation fixtures". The previous line in the same diff is 2875, and the uncommitted test diff adds exactly six `#[test]` functions (tests/tooling_grammar_test.rs:4474–4611), so the derivable count is 2875 + 6 = 2881, not 2883. The reported number therefore cannot be reconciled with the stated delta, which is the pattern the fake-completion check exists to catch. Fix: re-run the full gate and report the harvested number, or correct the prose and table together; do not hand-edit the count. — VERIFIED: arithmetic over the uncommitted REPORT diff and the six new test functions at tests/tooling_grammar_test.rs:4475, 4496, 4513, 4533, 4551, 4577.

3. [MINOR] phases/phase-075/REPORT.md:415 — the "Known gaps" bullet understates the limitation: it says only "a reference set does not include names written inside a second interpolation of the same text literal", but the implementation also omits interpolated uses from every other text literal in the file, and (per finding 1) omits them entirely when references are queried from an outer declaration. Fix: state the real limitation or implement global interpolation reference collection.

